# Apache Spark Performance Optimization Rules

## Cluster Configuration
- MUST configure Spark executor memory based on available cluster resources
- MUST set appropriate number of executors and cores per executor
- MUST configure Spark driver memory for large dataset processing
- MUST implement dynamic allocation for resource optimization
- MUST configure garbage collection settings for memory-intensive operations

## Data Partitioning Strategies
- MUST partition large fact tables by date and high-cardinality dimensions
- MUST use bucketing for frequently joined dimension tables
- MUST implement partition pruning for date-range queries
- MUST avoid partition skew by using appropriate partition keys
- MUST use partition discovery for efficient data reading

## Memory Management
- MUST configure appropriate memory fractions for storage and execution
- MUST implement broadcast joins for small dimension tables (< 10GB)
- MUST use off-heap memory for large datasets when available
- MUST implement proper caching strategies for frequently accessed data
- MUST monitor and tune memory usage for optimal performance

## Query Optimization
- MUST use columnar formats (Parquet) with appropriate compression
- MUST implement predicate pushdown for efficient filtering
- MUST use projection pushdown to read only required columns
- MUST optimize join strategies (broadcast, shuffle, sort-merge)
- MUST implement data skew handling with salting techniques

## Data Processing Patterns
- MUST use DataFrame API over RDDs for Catalyst optimizer benefits
- MUST implement incremental processing for large datasets
- MUST use checkpointing for long lineage chains
- MUST optimize shuffle operations with appropriate partition counts
- MUST implement data compaction for small files

## Monitoring and Debugging
- MUST implement Spark UI monitoring for performance analysis
- MUST log execution plans for query optimization
- MUST monitor resource utilization and GC metrics
- MUST implement custom metrics for business logic monitoring
- MUST use Spark history server for production monitoring

## Fault Tolerance
- MUST implement checkpointing for long-running operations
- MUST configure appropriate retry policies for transient failures
- MUST implement data recovery strategies for failed tasks
- MUST use write-ahead logs for critical data operations
- MUST implement proper error handling and recovery mechanisms